23483.sol:
The energy of light of wavelength $\lambda$ is given by
$E=h v=\frac{h c}{\lambda}$

Here, $h=$ Planck's constant $=6.63 \times 10^{-34} \mathrm{ J}-\mathrm{s}\begin{aligned}
c & =\text{ speed$ of $light }=3 \times 10^8 \mathrm{ m} / \mathrm{s} \\
E & =\text{ energy gap }=1.9 \mathrm{eV} \\
& =1.9 \times 1.6 \times 10^{-19} \mathrm{ J}
\end{aligned}$
Substituting the given values in Eq. (i), we get
$\begin{aligned}
\Rightarrow \lambda=\frac{6.63 \times 10^{-34} \times 3 \times 10^8}{1.9 \times 1.6 \times 10^{-19}} & =6.54 \times 10^{-7} \mathrm{ m} \\
& \approx 654 \mathrm{ nm}
\end{aligned}$
Thus, the wavelength of light emitted from LED will be $654 \mathrm{ nm} .$

